<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.apple.aslmanager</string>
	<key>Program</key>
	<string>/usr/sbin/aslmanager</string>
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>aslmanager</string>
	</array>
	<!--
	     DEMAND-LAUNCH PROBE (nextbsd-userland#143 follow-up).

	     #143 replaced MachServices with StartInterval 3600 and stubbed
	     asl_trigger_aslmanager() to a no-op. StartInterval only arms an
	     EVFILT_TIMER (core.c:2885) -- there is no dispatch at load -- so
	     aslmanager does not run for the first hour of any boot, and the
	     trigger that used to start it is gone. That is why it never runs.

	     This restores MachServices so launchd demand-launches the job, and
	     exists to answer one question in CI: does on-demand Mach-service
	     launch work now? When #143 removed it the answer was no, but the
	     two stubs behind that (#79: mach_port_get_set_status and
	     mach_port_get_attributes) were fixed by #83 on 08-29, and #78's
	     syslogd deadlock on 08-31 -- all BEFORE #143 landed at 08-31 22:56.
	     Nothing re-tested the path afterwards.

	     The boot-path stall #87 describes is NOT reintroduced: the call
	     site that caused it was removed separately by 3d3e575, 99 minutes
	     before #143, and stays removed (dbserver.c:152).

	     StandardErrorPath is the observable signal. launchd creates the
	     file when it spawns the job, and `launchctl list` cannot be used
	     for this -- job_export() (core.c:1095) always inserts
	     LastExitStatus, so a job that never ran and a job that exited 0
	     both print "-  0  com.apple.aslmanager".

	     EnableTransactions / EnablePressuredExit are dropped: both were
	     for the resident XPC listener that #143 deleted. aslmanager does
	     the work and exits.
	-->
	<key>MachServices</key>
	<dict>
		<key>com.apple.aslmanager</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/var/log/aslmanager.stderr</string>
	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>/var/log/aslmanager.stderr</string>
	<key>POSIXSpawnType</key>
	<string>Interactive</string>
</dict>
</plist>
